## How Big Is a 2 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond?

A 2 carat asscher cut diamond measures approximately 6.6×6.6mm face-up. That's roughly the width of a standard house key blade — genuinely impressive in person, but still smaller than most buyers expect when they hear the words "2 carats."

On a size 6 finger, a 2ct asscher covers about 39% of the finger width. A 2ct round at 8.2mm covers 48%. The asscher will look like a well-proportioned 1.5–1.7ct round in terms of sheer finger coverage — though the geometric step-cut character reads as larger than that surface area suggests.

This is where the Pavilion Weight Penalty becomes most visible to buyers who set their budget expecting round-equivalent presence. If you specifically want the asscher aesthetic but need finger coverage closer to a 2ct round, consider budgeting for 2.5ct in asscher.

For [asscher cut diamond engagement ring](/asscher-cut-diamond-engagement-rings) buyers, 2ct is the most popular size category. The hall-of-mirrors effect becomes genuinely dramatic at this size — at 1ct, the internal corridor effect is pretty but modest; at 2ct and above, it becomes the defining feature of the stone.

