## How Big Is a 3 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond?

A 3 carat asscher cut diamond measures approximately 7.7×7.7mm face-up. At that width, it extends nearly halfway across a size 6 finger — a statement piece by any standard.

The face-up area at 3ct is approximately 59.3mm². A 3ct round at 9.4mm delivers 69.4mm². That 10mm² gap is still visible but less jarring than at 1–2ct.

By this size, the asscher's geometric identity is so distinct that you stop comparing it to a round and start appreciating it on its own terms.

Natural GIA 3ct asscher starts at [$36,991](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28507345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Lab IGI D-IF at 3ct starts at [$8,849](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26682894?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The face-up measurement is 7.7mm in both cases.

