The size chart forces that math into the open.

![Lab vs natural asscher cut diamond price per mm chart — how much face-up size each budget buys](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-lab-vs-natural-price-per-mm.avif)

> **Farzana says:** If you showed me a 2.5ct lab asscher and a 2.5ct natural asscher side by side — no certificates — I couldn't tell you which is which. The step facets look the same. The hall-of-mirrors looks the same. The only real difference is in the paperwork and the price tag. At $6,449 vs $25,000+ for the same face-up size, that's a decision worth sitting with.

