## Master Comparison Matrix: Size Goal vs Budget

This matrix maps each size goal against the best natural and lab option, the face-up measurement, and the honest price comparison.

| Size Goal | Natural Option | Natural Price | Lab Option | Lab Price | mm Match | Savings |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| ~5.5mm (1ct presence) | [E-VS1 1.00ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $2,464 | [D-IF 1.52ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $2,795 | Lab: 6.1mm vs 5.5mm | Lab larger, $331 more |
| ~6.1mm (1.5ct presence) | [F-VVS1 1.07ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28382007?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $2,826 | [D-FL 1.98ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29230615?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $3,848 | Lab: 6.1mm vs 5.7mm | Lab larger, $1,022 more |
| ~6.6mm (2ct presence) | [G-VS2 2.21ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27103714?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $21,147 | [D-FL 2.00ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29446220?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $5,510 | Same 6.6mm | Lab saves $15,637 |
| ~7.2mm (2.5ct presence) | [E-VVS2 2.31ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16991410?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $31,990 | [D-IF 2.51ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28761376?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $6,449 | Lab: 7.2mm vs 7.0mm | Lab larger, saves $25,541 |
| ~7.7mm (3ct presence) | [F-VVS2 3.26ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28507345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $36,991 | [D-IF 3.00ct](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26682894?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $8,849 | Same 7.7mm | Lab saves $28,142 |

**What this means:** At the 1ct look, lab lets you buy a 1.5ct face-up stone for $331 more — a size upgrade, not a budget sacrifice. At the 2ct look, lab delivers the same 6.6mm appearance at $15,637 less. At the 3ct look, the gap reaches $28,142 for identical face-up measurements.

**Verdict:** For buyers optimizing face-up size at each price point, lab-grown asscher wins at every tier from 2ct onward in terms of pure size-per-dollar. At 1ct, the natural and lab prices are close enough that choice comes down to preference. Above 2ct, the math is structural — you get the same mm for a fraction of the natural price.

